.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt ADV462 6
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm adv462
.Nd Adventure 1.2 (462 points), from Honeywell's Phoenix Multics, 1980
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the version of Colossal Cave Adventure that ran on Honeywell's
Phoenix Multics system in 1980: Don Woods' 350-point game, in Gary
Palter's Multics Fortran port, with early material by Dave Platt
(rooms, treasures and creatures later found in his 550-point game).
There are seven treasures beyond Woods' fifteen, and a maximum score of
462.
.Pp
Type commands of one or two words, such as
.Dq get lamp
or
.Dq go north .
.Dq help
and
.Dq info
explain more.
Besides Woods' commands, this version understands:
.Bl -tag -width "suspend name"
.It Ic take all , drop all
pick up or put down everything at once
.It Ic fast , full
brief and full room descriptions
.It Ic listen
listen for creatures or water
.It Ic turns
how many turns you have taken
.It Ic hours
when the cave is open
.It Ic suspend Ar name
save the game under
.Ar name
(up to ten letters) and quit
.It Ic restore Ar name
continue a suspended game (in place of the current one)
.It Ic \&.
the version
.El
.Pp
A suspended game cannot be restored until the latency period (90 minutes
unless a wizard changes it) has passed, as on Multics.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ADV462_SAVEDIR
.It Ev ADV462_SAVEDIR
directory for suspended games (default
.Pa ~/.adv462 )
.It Ev ADV462_DIR
directory holding
.Pa adventure.newgame
.It Ev ADV462_DATA
path of the database
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/share/adv462/adventure.data
the game database, as printed in 1980 with its errors corrected
.It Pa /usr/local/share/adv462/adventure.newgame
the database already read in (saved in the wizard's
.Dq magic mode )
.It Pa /usr/games/adv462/
the writable game directory: an
.Pa adventure.data
or
.Pa adventure.newgame
here is used instead of the one in
.Pa /usr/local/share/adv462 ,
and magic mode saves its new
.Pa adventure.newgame
here
.It Pa ~/.adv462/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .adv462
suspended games
.El
.Sh HISTORY
The listings of this version were found among Jim Lippard's papers from
Phoenix Multics, transcribed, and made to run again in 2026.
See
.Lk https://github.com/lippard661/adv462
for the transcriptions and a list of the changes made.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Will Crowther
and
.An Don Woods
(the original game),
.An Gary Palter
(the Multics port),
.An Dave Platt
(the additional material),
.An Jim Lippard
(Phoenix Multics, 1980, and this revival).
